rce-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Number</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186228746 :question/problem "A librarian recorded the number of books read by each student in a reading club. The results are shown in the table below.\n\n| Student | Books read |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 1 | $5$ |\n| 2 | $8$ |\n| 3 | $6$ |\n| 4 | $9$ |\n| 5 | $4$ |\n| 6 | $7$ |\n| 7 | $10$ |\n\nWhat is the range of the number of books read among the $7$ students?" "A librarian recorded the number of books read by each student in a reading club. The results are shown in the table below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Student</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Books read</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">1</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">2</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">3</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">4</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">5</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">6</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">7</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nWhat is the range of the number of books read among the $7$ students?"] [:db/cas 17592186228747 :question/problem "| Streaming platform | Average monthly users (millions) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Platform X | $215$ |\n| Platform Y | $160$ |\n| Platform Z | $95$ |\n\nBased on the table above, how many more million users does Platform X have compared to Platform Z?" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Streaming platform</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Average monthly users (millions)</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Platform X</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$215$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Platform Y</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$160$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Platform Z</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$95$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nBased on the table above, how many more million users does Platform X have compared to Platform Z?"] [:db/cas 17592186228748 :question/problem "| Rent | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $7$ | $2$ |\n| $8$ | $3$ |\n| $9$ | $6$ |\n| $10$ | $5$ |\n| $11$ | $3$ |\n| $15$ | $1$ |\n\nThe table above shows the monthly rental costs (in hundreds of dollars) for $20$ units in an apartment complex. Which of the following gives the correct order of the mean, median, and mode of the rent amounts?\n\n1. $\\text{mode} = \\text{median} < \\text{mean}$\n2. $\\text{median} < \\text{mean}$\n3. $\\text{mean} < \\text{median}$\n4. $\\text{median} = \\text{mean} = \\text{mode}$" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Rent</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows the monthly rental costs (in hundreds of dollars) for $20$ units in an apartment complex. Which of the following gives the correct order of the mean, median, and mode of the rent amounts?\n\n1. $\\text{mode} = \\text{median} < \\text{mean}$\n2. $\\text{median} < \\text{mean}$\n3. $\\text{mean} < \\text{median}$\n4. $\\text{median} = \\text{mean} = \\text{mode}$"] [:db/cas 17592186228749 :question/problem "The table below summarizes the frequency of values in a data set.\n\n| Value | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $99$ | $3$ |\n| $101$ | $2$ |\n| $98$ | $4$ |\n| $100$ | $1$ |\n| $97$ | $1$ |\n\nWhat is the minimum value of the data set?" "The table below summarizes the frequency of values in a data set.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$99$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$101$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$98$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$100$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$97$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nWhat is the minimum value of the data set?"] [:db/cas 17592186228750 :question/problem "The table below shows the number of daily users for each of the $35$ different mobile apps reviewed in a tech report.\n\n| Number of daily users | Number of apps |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $100$ to $199$ | $5$ |\n| $200$ to $299$ | $4$ |\n| $300$ to $399$ | $6$ |\n| $400$ to $499$ | $5$ |\n| $500$ to $599$ | $6$ |\n| $600$ to $699$ | $5$ |\n| $700$ to $799$ | $4$ |\n\nWhich of the following could be the median number of daily users per app?\n\n1. $450$\n2. $350$\n3. $600$\n4. $250$" "The table below shows the number of daily users for each of the $35$ different mobile apps reviewed in a tech report.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Number of daily users</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Number of apps</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$100$ to $199$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$200$ to $299$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$300$ to $399$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$400$ to $499$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$500$ to $599$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$600$ to $699$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$700$ to $799$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nWhich of the following could be the median number of daily users per app?\n\n1. $450$\n2. $350$\n3. $600$\n4. $250$"] [:db/cas 17592186228751 :question/problem "| Value | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $9$ | $z$ |\n| $19$ | $3z$ |\n| $29$ | $6z$ |\n| $39$ | $3z$ |\n| $49$ | $z$ |\n\nThe frequency table above displays a set of data, where $z$ is a positive integer. By how much does the mean of the data set exceed the median?" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$z$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$19$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3z$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$29$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6z$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$39$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3z$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$49$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$z$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe frequency table above displays a set of data, where $z$ is a positive integer. By how much does the mean of the data set exceed the median?"] [:db/cas 17592186228752 :question/problem "Each of the following frequency tables represents a data set. Which one has the greatest mean? Round to two decimal places where necessary.\n\n**I.**\n\n| Value | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2$ | $1$ |\n| $5$ | $2$ |\n| $8$ | $2$ |\n| $11$ | $3$ |\n\n**II.**\n\n| Value | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2$ | $2$ |\n| $5$ | $2$ |\n| $8$ | $2$ |\n| $11$ | $2$ |\n\n**III.**\n\n| Value | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2$ | $3$ |\n| $5$ | $2$ |\n| $8$ | $2$ |\n| $11$ | $1$ |\n\n**IV.**\n\n| Value | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2$ | $2$ |\n| $5$ | $3$ |\n| $8$ | $2$ |\n| $11$ | $1$ |" "Each of the following frequency tables represents a data set. Which one has the greatest mean? Round to two decimal places where necessary.\n\n**I.**\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n**II.**\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n**III.**\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n**IV.**\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186228752 :question/worked-solution "The mean (or average) is calculated by dividing the sum of all the data values by the number of values.\n\nWe proceed to determine the mean of the data sets from each of the given frequency tables.\n\n- For the table\nValueFrequency$2$$1$$5$$2$$8$$2$$11$$3$\nthe mean of the data set is\n$$\n\\displaystyle mean|= (2(1) + 5(2) + 8(2) + 11(3))/(8); = \\frac{61}{8}; \\approx 7.63.\n$$\n- For the table\nValueFrequency$2$$2$$5$$2$$8$$2$$11$$2$\nthe mean of the data set is\n$$\n\\displaystyle mean|= (2(2) + 5(2) + 8(2) + 11(2))/(8); = \\frac{52}{8}; = 6.5.\n$$\n- For the table\nValueFrequency$2$$3$$5$$2$$8$$2$$11$$1$\nthe mean of the data set is\n$$\n\\displaystyle mean|= (2(3) + 5(2) + 8(2) + 11(1))/(8); = \\frac{43}{8}; \\approx 5.38.\n$$\n- For the table\nValueFrequency$2$$2$$5$$3$$8$$2$$11$$1$\nthe mean of the data set is\n$$\n\\displaystyle mean|= (2(2) + 5(3) + 8(2) + 11(1))/(8); = \\frac{46}{8}; = 5.75.\n$$\n- For the table\nValueFrequency$2$$2$$5$$2$$8$$1$$11$$3$\nthe mean of the data set is\n$$\n\\displaystyle mean|= (2(2) + 5(2) + 8(1) + 11(3))/(8); = \\frac{55}{8}; \\approx 6.88.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the frequency table whose data set has the greatest mean is as follows:\n\n| Value | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2$ | $1$ |\n| $5$ | $2$ |\n| $8$ | $2$ |\n| $11$ | $3$ |" "The mean (or average) is calculated by dividing the sum of all the data values by the number of values.\n\nWe proceed to determine the mean of the data sets from each of the given frequency tables.\n\n- For the table\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nthe mean of the data set is\n$$\n\\displaystyl