the desired probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(Exam1or3∣Perfect Score) &= \\frac{6 + 4}{12} \\\\\n&= \\frac{10}{12} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186228766 :question/problem "The table below shows the number of teachers in the English and History departments, categorized by whether they teach honors classes.\n\n|  | English | History |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Teach honors | $8$ | $5$ |\n| Do not teach honors | $4$ | $7$ |\n\nOne teacher from the English or History department is selected at random. If the teacher is from the English department, what is the probability that they do not teach honors classes?" "The table below shows the number of teachers in the English and History departments, categorized by whether they teach honors classes.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">English</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">History</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Teach honors</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Do not teach honors</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nOne teacher from the English or History department is selected at random. If the teacher is from the English department, what is the probability that they do not teach honors classes?"] [:db/cas 17592186228766 :question/worked-solution "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of English teachers who do not teach honors to the total number of English teachers. This is given by\n\n$$\nP(\\text{Not honors} \\mid \\text{English})=\\frac{\\text{Number of English not teaching honors}}{\\text{Total number of English}}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we can see that a total of\n\n$$\n8+4={\\color{red}12}\n$$\n\nEnglish teachers in the department. Of this amount, ${\\color{blue}4}$ do not teach honors.\n\n|  | English | History |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Teach honors | $8$ | $5$ |\n| Do not teach honors | $\\color{blue}4$ | $7$ |\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle P ( \\text{Not honors} ∣ \\text{English} ) & \\displaystyle  = \\frac{ {\\color{blue}4}}{ {\\color{red}12}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1 \\cdot  4}{3 \\cdot  4}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1 \\cdot  \\cancel{4}}{3 \\cdot  \\cancel{4}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = \\frac{1}{3} .\\end{array}}\n$$" "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of English teachers who do not teach honors to the total number of English teachers. This is given by\n\n$$\nP(\\text{Not honors} \\mid \\text{English})=\\frac{\\text{Number of English not teaching honors}}{\\text{Total number of English}}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we can see that a total of\n\n$$\n8+4={\\color{red}12}\n$$\n\nEnglish teachers in the department. Of this amount, ${\\color{blue}4}$ do not teach honors.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">English</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">History</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Teach honors</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Do not teach honors</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFF8E5\">$\\color{blue}4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle P ( \\text{Not honors} ∣ \\text{English} ) & \\displaystyle  = \\frac{ {\\color{blue}4}}{ {\\color{red}12}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1 \\cdot  4}{3 \\cdot  4}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1 \\cdot  \\cancel{4}}{3 \\cdot  \\cancel{4}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = \\frac{1}{3} .\\end{array}}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186228767 :question/problem "A veterinary clinic tracked incoming calls on a single day, recording whether callers inquired about appointments or pet food. The results are shown in the table below.\n\n|  | Pet food request | No pet food request | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Appointment request | $55$ | $345$ | $400$ |\n| No Appointment request | $45$ | $55$ | $100$ |\n| **Total** | **$100$** | **$400$** | **$500$** |\n\nIf a caller who asked about pet food is selected at random, what is the probability that the caller also asked about an appointment?" "A veterinary clinic tracked incoming calls on a single day, recording whether callers inquired about appointments or pet food. The results are shown in the table below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Pet food request</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">No pet food request</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Appointment request</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$55$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$345$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$400$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">No Appointment request</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$45$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$55$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$100$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$400$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$500$</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIf a caller who asked about pet food is selected at random, what is the probability that the caller also asked about an appointment?"] [:db/cas 17592186228767 :question/worked-solution "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of callers who asked about pet food and an appointment to the total number of callers who asked about pet food. This is given by\n\n$$\n\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\! P(\\text{Appointment} \\mid \\text{Pet food}) = \\frac{\\text{Number of requests for appointment and pet food}}{\\text{Total number of requests for pet food}}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we can see that there are a total of ${\\color{red}100}$ callers who asked about pet food. Of this amount, ${\\color{blue}55}$ also asked about an appointment.\n\n|  | Pet food request | No pet food request | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Appointment request | $\\color{blue}55$ | $345$ | $400$ |\n| No Appointment request | $45$ | $55$ | $100$ |\n| **Total** | ${\\color{red}100}$ | **$400$** | **$500$** |\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(Appointment∣Pet food) &= \\frac{55}{100} \\\\\n&= 0.55\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of callers who asked about pet food and an appointment to the total number of callers who asked about pet food. This is given by\n\n$$\n\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\! P(\\text{Appointment} \\mid \\text{Pet food}) = \\frac{\\text{Number of requests for appointment and pet food}}{\\text{Total number of requests for pet food}}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we can see that there are a total of ${\\color{red}100}$ callers who asked about pet food. Of this amount, ${\\color{blue}55}$ also asked about an appointment.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Pet food request</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">No pet food request</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Appointment request</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFF8E5\">$\\color{blue}55$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$345$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$400$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">No Appointment request</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$45$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$55$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFF8E5\">${\\color{red}100}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$400$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$500$</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(Appointment∣Pet food) &= \\frac{55}{100} \\\\\n&= 0.55\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186228771 :question/problem "In a midterm exam, each student receives a score between $50$ and $100$. The table below shows the score distribution for the $13$ students in Class $M$ and the $11$ students in Class $N$.\n\n| Score | Class $M$ | Class $N$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $