"><strong>$125$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$132$</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows the number of students from two schools who completed coding certifications. Of the students who completed a coding certification in $2018$, which of the following represents the fraction of students who were from Riverside?"] [:db/cas 17592186229357 :question/problem "For a wildlife study, Nora recorded whether deer were spotted during morning and evening hikes over $10$ weekends. Her results are shown in the table below.\n\n|  | Deer spotted | No deer spotted | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Morning hikes | $11$ | $9$ | $20$ |\n| Evening hikes | $6$ | $14$ | $20$ |\n| **Total** | **$17$** | **$23$** | **$40$** |\n\nIf one of the hikes on which no deer were spotted is selected at random, what is the probability the hike was in the evening?" "For a wildlife study, Nora recorded whether deer were spotted during morning and evening hikes over $10$ weekends. Her results are shown in the table below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Deer spotted</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">No deer spotted</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Morning hikes</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Evening hikes</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>Total</