 of undergraduates (freshmen, sophomores, juniors, and seniors combined) who preferred morning classes and the percentage of graduate students who preferred morning classes?" "A total of $34, 852$ students study at a certain university. The university conducted a survey among a randomly chosen sample of $1, 200$ students about their preference for morning or evening classes. The results are shown in the table below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Morning</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Evening</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">No Preference</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Freshmen and Sophomores</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$280$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$190$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$500$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Juniors and Seniors</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$210$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$150$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$40$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$400$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Graduates</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$120$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$100$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$80$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$300$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Total</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$610$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$440$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$150$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1, 200$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nWhich of the following is closest to the difference between the percentage of undergraduates (freshmen, sophomores, juniors, and seniors combined) who preferred morning classes and the percentage of graduate students who preferred morning classes?"] [:db/cas 17592186229458 :question/problem "| Company | $2015$ | $2016$ | $2017$ | $2018$ | $2019$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Acme Corp | $89$ | $83$ | $91$ | $87$ | $85$ |\n| Zenith Inc. | $78$ | $80$ | $82$ | $100$ | $102$ |\n\nThe table above shows the number of employees at two companies in each of the five years. No employee worked at both companies.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true about the number of employees over the $5$ years shown?\n\n1. The mean number from Acme Corp is greater than the mean number from Zenith Inc.\n2. The median number from Acme Corp is greater than the median number from Zenith Inc." "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Company</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$2015$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$2016$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$2017$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$2018$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$2019$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Acme Corp</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$89$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$83$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$91$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$87$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$85$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Zenith Inc.</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$78$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$80$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$82$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$100$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$102$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows the number of employees at two companies in each of the