-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$32 - 34$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$34 - 36$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$36 - 38$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$38 - 40$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."] [:db/cas 17592186229548 :question/problem "| Value | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $12 - 14$ | $3$ |\n| $15 - 16$ | $5$ |\n| $17 - 18$ | $4$ |\n| $19 - 20$ | $2$ |\n| $21 - 22$ | $3$ |\n\nThe frequency table above shows the number of values in a dataset that fall into each group. What is the smallest possible value of the range?\n\nThe smallest possible range is\n{{field-1}}." "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12 - 14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15 - 16$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$17 - 18$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$19 - 20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$21 - 22$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe frequency table above shows the number of values in a dataset that fall into each group. What is the smallest possible value of the range?\n\nThe smallest possible range is\n{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186229552 :question/problem "| **Alice** | $4.2$ | $3.8$ | $3.2$ | $4.0$ | $4.5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Bob** | $x$ | $4.6$ | $4.0$ | $3.8$ | $4.8$ |\n\nAlice and Bob each attempted the math test five times, and their scores are represented in the table above. The mean score for Bob's attempts was $0.5$ greater than the mean score for Alice's attempts. What is the value of $x$?\n\n$x =$\n{{field-1}}" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>Alice</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>Bob</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.8$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nAlice and Bob each attempted the math test five times, and their scores are represented in the table above. The mean score for Bob's attempts was $0.5$ greater than the mean score for Alice's attempts. What is the value of $x$?\n\n$x =$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186229621 :question/problem "A table shows the number of subscribers to a newsletter for six different years.\n\n| Year | Subscribers |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2015$ | $3600$ |\n| $2016$ | $4200$ |\n| $2017$ | $5000$ |\n| $2018$ | $4600$ |\n| $2019$ | $3800$ |\n| $2021$ | $3000$ |\n\nWhat was the percentage decrease in subscribers from $2017$ to $2021$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." "A table shows the number of subscribers to a newsletter for six different years.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Year</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Subscribers</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2015$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3600$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2016$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4200$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2017$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5000$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2018$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4600$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2019$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3800$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2021$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3000$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nWhat was the percentage decrease in subscribers from $2017$ to $2021$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."] [:db/cas 17592186231379 :question/problem "| $x$ | $f(x)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $3$ |\n| $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $0$ | $5$ |\n| $1$ | $-1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of $f$ on the set $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.$ Use the table to compute\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\" data-cell-align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above gives values of $f$ on the set $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.$ Use the table to compute\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186231388 :question/problem "A tour guide has created a list of various ancient artifacts located inside and outside a cave in a park. The distance is measured from the entrance of the cave, with positive values representing distances outside the cave and negative values representing distances inside the cave. The data is shown below.\n\n| Artifact Point | Distance (m) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| A | $-10$ |\n| C | $20$ |\n| B | $-50$ |\n| D | $60$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. Point A is $10\\,\\textrm{m}$ inside the cave.\n2. Point A is further inside the cave than point D.\n3. Point A is further inside the cave than any other point." "A tour guide has created a list of various ancient artifacts located inside and outside a cave in a park. The distance is measured from the entrance of the cave, with positive values representing distances outside the cave and negative values representing distances inside the cave. The data is shown below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\